From d3a25a4c33aaaf40ee41b0f8fb049ae2e94fe54e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:23:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] chore(beads): purge dead beads-bootstrap/health-check runtime
 wiring

lib/beads-bootstrap.js and lib/beads-health-check.js had zero live
callers: their only consumer was bin/forge.js's inline `command ===
'setup'` legacy implementation, which the lib/commands/ registry
dispatcher intercepts and returns from first (bin/forge.js:1771-1774),
making that inline block dead code on every current CLI invocation.

Delete both files and their tests, and drop bin/forge.js's require of
beads-health-check (needed so removing the file doesn't crash module
load) plus the dead health-check block inside initializeBeads(). Fix
the package-distribution test's required-lib-modules list to match.

Left in place (live, in-scope, or protected):
- lib/beads-setup.js: isBeadsInitialized() is used by the explicit
  --issue-backend beads opt-in passthrough (lib/forge-issues.js).
- lib/adapters/beads-kernel-compat.js: the migrator's Beads<->Kernel
  mapping layer, live-used by lib/commands/migrate.js (a different,
  protected agent's file) and lib/kernel/broker.js /
  projection-jsonl-writer.js.
- lib/orientation.js, lib/insights.js, lib/status/beads-snapshot.js:
  read-only .beads/*.jsonl compat projections that already return []
  when the file is absent -- no shell-out, no stderr noise.
- lib/commands/validate.js, lib/patch-intent.js,
  lib/protected-state-surfaces.js: '.beads' only appears as a
  directory-exclusion/protection-path literal, not a live dependency.

Strengthened test/e2e/fresh-clone-no-beads.test.js: switched the forge()
runner from execFileSync to spawnSync so stderr is captured on the
success path too, added a `forge status --json` call, and asserted no
captured stderr matches /beads/i -- proving the kernel-primary/no-.beads/
acceptance criterion holds for stderr noise, not just bd/dolt shell-outs.

Refs: 726fc438 (beads runtime purge), 8e38896c (stderr noise)
